      <title>Race to replant five South African baobabs after export blocked</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/19/baobab-five-trees-south-africa-dug-up-export-blocked-georgia-aoe</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The trees, intended for an unnamed buyer in Georgia, were reportedly dug up without the necessary permits&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Environmentalists in South Africa are racing to replant five centuries-old baobabs after the 20-tonne trees were dug up by an exporter, who tried to ship them thousands of miles to Georgia.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The baobabs arrived at a reserve in Timbavati, in north-eastern South Africa, on Wednesday, where they will be replanted and supported by cables to help them recover. The trees had been stranded at a warehouse in Durban since July, when they were intercepted by authorities who said they had been moved without the necessary permissions.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/19/baobab-five-trees-south-africa-dug-up-export-blocked-georgia-aoe"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
