      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/us-sanctions-icj-judges-myanmar-genocide-ruling-israel-gaza-court</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A ruling against Myanmar could set precedent for court’s judgment on Israel’s actions in Gaza&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fears are growing that the US could impose sanctions on judges at the international court of justice, including this year’s &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/navanethem-navi-pillay-wins-nobel-peace-prize"&gt;Nobel peace prize winner, Navi Pillay&lt;/a&gt;, if the &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/15/myanmar-rohingya-genocide-icj"&gt;court rules on Thursday that the Myanmar government committed genocide&lt;/a&gt; against the Rohingya.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ICJ has never found a state responsible for committing genocide, and a significant factor in previous cases has been how to prove “intent” in a crime defined as acts committed with the “intent to destroy, in whole or in part” a national, ethnical, racial or religious group.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/us-sanctions-icj-judges-myanmar-genocide-ruling-israel-gaza-court"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
